# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository. Git still checks files
# out as LF on every platform (eol=lf), which is fine for Windows tooling
# here since nothing in this project (Python, TOML, Markdown, YAML, JSON)
# requires CRLF to function correctly on Windows. Git's text auto-detection
# is reliable for all file types actually in this repo, so one blanket
# rule covers everything — no need to repeat it per extension.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Native Windows scripts, if any are ever added, keep CRLF for tools that
# expect it (e.g. cmd.exe batch files).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never let Git normalize binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
